{"resourceIdentifier":"2410","resourceName":"REFORESTATION OF DEGRADED FOREST RESERVE AREAS IN GHANA, WEST AFRICA","description":"Miro Forestry has over 10,000 hectares of standing plantations, expanding this plantation area at a rate of 3,000 hectares per year and producing sustainable timber products including plywood, rotary veneer, poles, sawn timber, and wood biomass.\r\nThe plantations are Forest Stewardship Council™ (FSC™) certified meaning the voluntary compliance with the international gold standard of responsible forest management.\r\nThe plantation in Ghana is around 7° north of the equator and has a tropical climate with average monthly temperatures ranging between 24°C and 28°C and annual rainfall between 1,300 - 1,650mm. The rains predominantly fall in May, June, July, and September with the driest hottest months being December through to March.\r\nThe land on which the company is establishing plantation forests was severely degraded during the 1980s and 1990s by agricultural clearing and heavy logging. The land has been designated a forestry reserve, and the Ghanaian Forestry Commission is very supportive of foreign investment being deployed to reforest the area.\r\nMiro Forestry aims to conform to high environmental, ethical, financial and social standards, and achieve international forestry certification on all plantations. It aims to be the preferred partner for local communities, the national government, and international development and finance.","location":{"latitude":7.024102,"longitude":-1.212169},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-03-03","endExclusive":"2021-04-03","endInclusive":"2021-04-02"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2410"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ashanti"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Miro Forestry Developments Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"London, United Kingdom"},{"type":"string","value":"44(0)7899074158"},{"type":"string","value":"info@miroforestry.com"},{"type":"string","value":"https://www.miroforestry.com/"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification approval requested"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2410"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2410"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"46229"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":66458}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"7086 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AENOR CONFIA, S.A. (UNIPERSONAL)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"01/03/2022"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 24/03/2016 - 23/03/2046"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=51251&IDKEY=fiofj09234rm9oq4jndsma80vcalksdjf98cxkjaf90823nmq3n70675129","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"210210_Miro_AR_Ghana_PDD.pdf","uploadDate":"2021-03-03T21:11:49.43Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=50151&IDKEY=88723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq0869158229","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"302583_33791_contract_2 (1).pdf","uploadDate":"2020-12-29T16:51:56.76Z"}]},{"code":"VCS_REGISTRATION_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Registration Documents","documents":[{"uri